speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, pursuant to Standing Order 43, 1 seek the unanimous consent of the House to move a motion on a matter of urgent and pressing necessity.
In view of the fact that the 30 employees of Quebec city radio station CJRP have been fighting since September 1974 to obtain a collective agreement and were certified as a union in July 1975; and in view of the fact that this union has no guarantee that it will be covered by the provisions of the Canada Labour Code, as amended by Bill C-8, providing for the settlement of first collective agreements and this, not because of the principle of the act, but because of its retroactive effect to December 31, 1975, I move, seconded by the hon. member for Winnipeg North Centre (Mr. Knowles);
That the House request the government to amend the first subsection of section 171.1 of the Canada Labour Code and replace "December 31, 1975" by "July 31, 1975".
